/A 1277 0 R
/Alt (Five-panel infographic summarising ESOT position statements on AI in transplantation: First panel - high quality AI development requires collaboration, high quality data, and methodological rigour; second panel - ethical considerations include equity, access to care, and data privacy; third panel - regulatory considerations require compliance with EU medical device and AI legislation; fourth panel - responsible adoption emphasises AI literacy, human oversight and expertise, and performance-based trust. Fifth panel - participatory design ensures that clinical needs and patient preferences are at the heart of AI development.)
